# The retrieval layer's four answers for this repository.
# The contract is infra/retrieval/CONTRACT.md in promontory-studio/plover-context.

# `entry` is left at its default, AGENTS.md, and here that is not the ceiling's doing: README.md is
# 3,969 B and would still be under 12,000 B with a routing section inside it, which is how
# finca-code and promo-code route. What decides it is audience and vocabulary. README.md is the
# front page for the people this repository is structured for — invited health-literacy experts, and
# a reviewer reading it cold — and CLAUDE.md's wording rule governs exactly that framing copy. The
# routing vocabulary is node identifiers: `patientHypothesis`, `labData`, `markerGroups`. CLAUDE.md
# puts those out of its scope as data-model identifiers rather than framing copy, so they are
# admissible, and keeping them out of README.md keeps the rule's subject clean. README.md's own
# "Map of the docs" already names the four root documents, which is the half an expert wants.

# `out` is left at its default, HEADINGS.md.

# Everything but the two forge forms under .github/. Forty-four documents: the eight at the root and
# the thirty-six nodes of finding-dag/, whose prose is the content this repository exists to hold
# rather than fixture data. `[!.]*.md` is the one-glob way to say that — fnmatch's `*` crosses `/`,
# so a leading `[!.]` drops every dot-directory and keeps every depth below a named one.
scope = [!.]*.md

# A hit may be answered with the line that matched. This repository is public by design, carries no
# app code and no credential, and holds no person's record: README.md says so as the reason invited
# experts can be given access at all. A node's prose is an instruction to a reasoning step, and the
# values inside it are examples written to show what a rationale has to name — not readings taken
# from anybody. What a line carries is therefore the rule itself, and the rule is usually the
# answer: ARCHITECTURE.md's lint rules and frontmatter keys are stated line by line, and a node's
# `## Reasoning` block is a sequence of prohibitions where the enclosing heading says only
# "Reasoning" and the line says what is actually forbidden.
quote = line
